    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "349c448e_6fab8129",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 3206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076971
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T17:19:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "All of this is implemented by the OEM so it\u0027s from /vendor (via the KeyMaster or KeyMint HALs) and OEMs don\u0027t have to upgrade that partition (but some do) when they upgrade /system to Android 12. We will start requiring these features to be set starting with Android 12 and we\u0027ll check that that in CTS (CL:1626759).\n\nSo unfortunately this is more complicated than I like but there\u0027s nothing to do about this I\u0027m afraid. What I\u0027ve added in the latest PS is the following:\n\n This feature version is guaranteed to be set for all devices launching with\n Android 12 and may be set on devices launching with an earlier version. If\n the feature version is set, it will at least have the value 40. If it\u0027s not\n set the device may have a version of hardware-backed keystore but it may\n not support all features listed above.",
      "parentUuid": "047b42c2_4bb30aaa",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3205,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3206,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "e55be4061ded9849a2a931d88ed07d9868d8aded",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "431a78ab_931fa36a",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 3206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010050
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T18:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main issue with the \"all devices launching with\" language is that there\u0027s no way for an app to query that, so it basically just boils down to \"may not be set\".\n\nIt\u0027d be great if we could require OEMs to set a feature flag on upgrade at least (since it sounds like no actual new feature development work would be needed), but I know the various vendor upgrade support requirements can make that difficult at times.  Is there any way we could set it automatically for the OEM?",
      "parentUuid": "349c448e_6fab8129",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3205,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3206,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "e55be4061ded9849a2a931d88ed07d9868d8aded",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1d6fe700_63cc4be8",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 3206,
      "author": {
        "id": 1076971
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-03-24T19:04:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right. So \"may not be set\" really means that the application isn\u0027t guaranteed anything wrt. whether this is implemented in Secure Hardware or not. For all we know the device could have no KeyMaster at all or an ancient one (KeyMaster 1, 2, or 3).\n\nNote that the APIs for e.g. AES, HMAC, EC, RSA operations with AndroidKeystore provider still work though, they just aren\u0027t backed by secure hardware - the app can check for this through attestations or android.security.keystore.KeyInfo. getSecurityLevel().\n\nSo if the app is running on a device where FEATURE_HARDWARE_KEYSTORE isn\u0027t set it can always find out if Secure Hardware is available by simply just trying to create the key and then check KeyInfo. They can then bail at runtime if the key isn\u0027t created in secure hardware.\n\nThe main reason for adding FEATURE_HARDWARE_KEYSTORE is for apps which won\u0027t run on devices that don\u0027t have the necessary secure hardware. By using this, they can be filtered in the play store so they won\u0027t appear on devices without it.\n\nWith this in mind, I\u0027m not sure there\u0027s a lot of value of forcing OEMs to set this or automatically set it for them. I\u0027ll let Shawn chime in on this as well.",
      "parentUuid": "431a78ab_931fa36a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3205,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 3206,
        "endChar": 68
      },
      "revId": "e55be4061ded9849a2a931d88ed07d9868d8aded",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "90d8f3d6_def2b718",
        "filename": "core/java/android/content/pm/PackageManager.java",
